],"recent_en":"Hengyuan completed a fund-raising exercise in late October 2026 and has continued to list new shares from warrant conversions; it also appointed Erkki Ranta as CEO, with changes in substantial shareholder holdings. Revenue and net profit both grew quarter-on-quarter in Q2 2026.","notable_en":["The company announced a new issue of securities for fund-raising on 30 October 2026.","Erkki Tapio Ranta returned as CEO on 1 October 2026, while Yin Lujiang ceased as principal officer the same day.","The company declared a first interim dividend for FY2026 and released quarterly results for the period ended 30 June 2026."],"risks_en":["The company continues to increase its issued share capital through warrant conversions, with latest issued shares at about 602 million.","Substantial shareholders Heng Yuan Holdings Limited and Malaysia Hengyuan International Limited reported changes in their holdings on 30 October 2026."],"earnings_en":"Q2 2026 revenue was MYR 5,435,086,000, up 17.5% QoQ and 55.7% YoY; net profit was MYR 600,541,000, up 14.3% QoQ, with a net margin of 11.0% versus 11.4% in the prior quarter."}